---
kind: lore
id: skerry.keeperLog
title: Skerry Rock light, keeper's log
series: keeperLog
---

<entry id="keeperLog1" on="examine" target="item.logbook" category="note" title="14 October, afternoon" priority="30" once="run">
  @elias{code="0010"}: 14th Oct. 4 p.m. Glass falling fast. Wind SW, backing. Lit at 5.10, dusk.
  @elias{code="0020"}: A. Pell still ashore, Mrs Hale sends word she is poorly. No supper tin today. I shall manage.
  ::assert{placedBy(logbook, elias, lantern, dusk)}
</entry>

<entry id="keeperLog2" on="examine" target="item.logbook" category="note" title="14 October, night" priority="20" once="run" when="entry.keeperLog1.read">
  @elias{code="0010"}: 11.40 p.m. Clockwork seized. Turning the lens by hand. Salt on the glass so thick the beam is nothing.
  @elias{code="0020"}: Going out on the gallery to wipe it. God keep the ships off the Teeth tonight.
  ::assert{placedBy(logbook, elias, gallery, midnight)}
</entry>

<entry id="keeperLog3" on="examine" target="item.logbook" category="note" title="15 October, small hours" priority="10" once="run" when="entry.keeperLog2.read">
  @narrator{code="0010"}: The next entry is in a different hand: rounder, pressed hard enough to tear the paper.
  @ada{code="0010" vo}: 2.10. Light relit. He is not on the gallery. The rail is gone on the seaward side. I have looked everywhere. A.P.
  ::assert{placedBy(logbook, ada, lantern, midnight)}
</entry>

<entry id="keeperLogStub" on="examine" target="item.logbook" category="note" title="A torn stub" when="entry.keeperLog3.read">
  @narrator{code="0010"}: After the last entry, a page has been torn out. Only the stub is left, and the word "tell".
</entry>
